    <!-- THREE METRICS SECTION -->
    <section class="content-section" id="three-metric">
      <h2>The Three Core Real Estate Investment Metrics</h2>
      <p>Every US rental property should be evaluated with all three metrics before purchase. They answer different questions and together give you the full picture.</p>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:1.25rem;margin-top:1.25rem;">

        <div style="background:#f0fdf4;border:1.5px solid #bbf7d0;border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem;">
          <div style="font-size:1.6rem;margin-bottom:.5rem;">📊</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 .5rem;color:#065f46;font-size:1.05rem;">Cap Rate</h3>
          <p style="font-size:.9rem;color:#475569;margin:0 0 .75rem;line-height:1.65;">Unlevered return — measures NOI relative to full property value. Financing-independent. Use it to <strong>compare properties</strong> across markets regardless of how they're financed.</p>
          <code style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d1fae5;border-radius:6px;padding:.6rem .85rem;font-size:.82rem;color:#065f46;">NOI / Property Value × 100</code>
          <a href="/real-estate/cap-rate-calculator" style="display:block;margin-top:.85rem;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:700;color:#059669;text-decoration:none;">Calculate Cap Rate →</a>
        </div>

        <div style="background:#eff6ff;border:1.5px solid #bfdbfe;border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem;">
          <div style="font-size:1.6rem;margin-bottom:.5rem;">🏠</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 .5rem;color:#1e3a8a;font-size:1.05rem;">Rental Yield</h3>
          <p style="font-size:.9rem;color:#475569;margin:0 0 .75rem;line-height:1.65;">Income relative to property value. Gross yield ignores expenses; net yield includes them all. Use it to <strong>screen markets</strong> — Cleveland 11.3%, US avg 6.71%, NYC 3–4%.</p>
          <code style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid #bfdbfe;border-radius:6px;padding:.6rem .85rem;font-size:.82rem;color:#1e3a8a;">Annual Rent / Property Value × 100</code>
          <a href="/real-estate/rental-yield-calculator" style="display:block;margin-top:.85rem;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:700;color:#2563eb;text-decoration:none;">Calculate Rental Yield →</a>
        </div>

        <div style="background:#faf5ff;border:1.5px solid #e9d5ff;border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem;">
          <div style="font-size:1.6rem;margin-bottom:.5rem;">💵</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 .5rem;color:#4c1d95;font-size:1.05rem;">Cash-on-Cash Return</h3>
          <p style="font-size:.9rem;color:#475569;margin:0 0 .75rem;line-height:1.65;">Levered return — measures annual after-mortgage cash flow relative only to <strong>your cash invested</strong>. The definitive metric for evaluating a specific deal with your financing.</p>
          <code style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid #e9d5ff;border-radius:6px;padding:.6rem .85rem;font-size:.82rem;color:#4c1d95;">Cash Flow / Cash Invested × 100</code>
          <a href="/real-estate/cash-on-cash-return-calculator" style="display:block;margin-top:.85rem;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:700;color:#7c3aed;text-decoration:none;">Calculate Cash-on-Cash Return →</a>
        </div>

        <div style="background:#fefce8;border:1.5px solid #fef08a;border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem;">
          <div style="font-size:1.6rem;margin-bottom:.5rem;">🔄</div>
          <h3 style="margin:0 0 .5rem;color:#854d0e;font-size:1.05rem;">BRRRR Strategy Engine</h3>
          <p style="font-size:.9rem;color:#475569;margin:0 0 .75rem;line-height:1.65;">Buy, Rehab, Rent, Refinance, Repeat. Calculate cash-out refi proceeds, capital recycled %, cash left in deal, and infinite cash-on-cash return.</p>
          <code style="display:block;background:#fff;border:1px solid #fef08a;border-radius:6px;padding:.6rem .85rem;font-size:.82rem;color:#854d0e;">Recycled % = Refi Cash / All-In Capital × 100</code>
          <a href="/real-estate/brrrr-calculator" style="display:block;margin-top:.85rem;font-size:.85rem;font-weight:700;color:#ca8a04;text-decoration:none;">Calculate BRRRR Deal →</a>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div style="background:#fffbeb;border-left:4px solid #d97706;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0;font-size:.94rem;color:#92400e;line-height:1.6;">
        ⚠️ <strong>2026 rate environment note:</strong> With 30-year mortgage rates at 7–7.5%, many properties that show good rental yield and cap rate actually produce <em>negative cash-on-cash return</em> when financed. Always run all three metrics. Focus on markets with gross yields above 8% (Cleveland, Memphis, Cincinnati) to achieve positive CoC at current rates.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2026 US MARKET SNAPSHOT -->
    <section class="content-section" id="market-snapshot">
      <h2><%= currentYear %> US Rental Market Snapshot</h2>
      <p>These benchmark figures help you quickly assess whether a property's numbers are competitive for its market.</p>
      <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;border:1px solid #e8edf5;margin-bottom:1rem;">
        <thead><tr style="background:#059669;color:#fff;">
          <th style="padding:11px 14px;text-align:left;font-size:.86rem;">Market</th>
          <th style="padding:11px 14px;text-align:left;font-size:.86rem;">Gross Yield</th>
          <th style="padding:11px 14px;text-align:left;font-size:.86rem;">Est. CoC (20% down)</th>
          <th style="padding:11px 14px;text-align:left;font-size:.86rem;">Strategy</th>
